          %h3#string_cosmic_inflation String cosmic inflation
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inflaton"} inflaton
            field for models of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosmic+inflation"} cosmic inflation
            field can be modeled by various effects, such as
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+string"} open string
              stretching between
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-brane"} D-brane
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anti+D-brane"} anti D-brane
              pairs.
          %p For a review and further pointers to the literature see at
          %ul
            %li
              Cliff Burgess, M. Cicoli, F. Quevedo,
              %em String Inflation After Planck 2013
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1306.3512"}> arXiv:1306.3512
              )
          %h3#axion_phenomenology Axion phenomenology
          %p
            On stringy
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axion"} axion
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/phenomenology"} phenomenology
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Joseph P. Conlon, M.C. David Marsh,
                %em Searching for a 0.1-1 keV Cosmic Axion Background
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1305.3603"}> arXiv:1305.3603
                )
              %blockquote
                %p
                  Primordial decays of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stabilization"} moduli
                  at
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi z
                        %mo ∼
                        %msup
                          %mn 10
                          %mn 12
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z \sim 10^{12}
                  naturally generate a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dark+radiation"} dark radiation
                  Cosmic Axion Background (CAB) with
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0.1
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                        %mi keV
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0.1 - 1 keV
                  energies. This CAB can be detected through axion-
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/photon"} photon
                  conversion in astrophysical
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/magnetic+fields"} magnetic fields
                  to give quasi-thermal excesses in the extreme ultraviolet and soft X-ray bands. Substantial and observable luminosities may be generated even for axion-photon couplings
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo ≪
                          %msup
                            %mn 10
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mn 11
                          %msup
                            %mi GeV
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mn 1
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ll 10^{-11} GeV^{-1}
